=== A. MATCHED-PAIR ANALYSIS (the primary test) ===
   Within pairs matched on public coordinability, does the model bet more on
   the stimulus where its OWN policy actually coordinates better?

   PRIMARY: one joint payoff-response model per pair -
     attempt ~ is_high + safe_payoff   (logistic, trials from all payoffs)
   tested by permuting the high/low stimulus label WITHIN each payoff stratum,
   so the payoff response is preserved and the four payoff levels contribute
   one statistic, not four. The per-payoff differences printed underneath are
   DESCRIPTIVE ONLY: they are the same two stimuli and the same two Stage-A
   estimates re-tested four times, so they are not independent replications.

